.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-dupes 1  "dfdu-dupes " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-dupes \- Scan a directory and list the files with identical contents (size, then partial hash, then SHA\-256), the most space to free first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu dupes\fR [\fB\-\-min\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-mft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a directory and list the files with identical contents (size, then partial hash, then SHA\-256), the most space to free first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR [default: 1MiB]
Compare only files of at least this size (`1MiB`, `100KB`)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output: table or json (schema/dupes.v1.json)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR
Groups to print, the most space to free first [default: all]
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Threads reading files [default: 4; 1 on spinning disks]
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-mft\fR
Windows, as administrator: read each NTFS volume\*(Aqs master file table instead of listing its directories, which is much faster on large volumes. Volumes whose table cannot be read are listed as usual
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

